      "date": "2026-09-01",
      "kind": "correction",
      "text": "SKILL.md (444 lines, ~70-90K tokens) is read cold and in full at the start of EVERY run, including quick runs, even though ~90% of it is deep-mode-only reference material (macro dispatch, quality/tax/cycle triggers, dashboard build spec). This is the single largest fixed orchestrator cost and it recurs daily. The codebase already solved the identical problem once for smith_math.py -- split from a 4,085-line monolith into smith_core/risk/ledger/memory/lifecycle/math specifically because 'state.json is read every run and sliced into every prompt' -- but SKILL.md itself never got the same treatment, and reference/dashboard.md + reference/proposals-engine.md already prove the pattern works. Fixed 2026-09-01: SKILL.md restructured into a lean quick-mode core plus reference/deep-mode-dispatch.md (macro/quality/tax/cycle/earnings/catalyst dispatch rules) and reference/quick-vs-deep.md is not needed -- the split follows the existing reference/ convention. Generalise: any prompt or state file that is loaded in full on every run, regardless of mode, is a candidate for this split the moment most of its content only applies to one mode.",
