      "text": "Price fetches happen in overlapping waves instead of one consolidated batch. Measured on the 2026-09-01 quick sweep: market inputs (9 tickers) -> holdings (30 tickers) -> score-probe (18 tickers, ~12 overlapping with holdings) -> stops-probe (57 tickers, ~25 overlapping with holdings) -- 4 separate yfinance batch calls with heavy ticker overlap, when the union of every ticker any stage would eventually need (macro proxies + held names + score/stops-probe named tickers) was knowable before the first fetch. Fixed 2026-09-01: SKILL.md section 2.5b now instructs fetching the full known ticker union in ONE batched pass at the top of PREFETCH, caching it in holdings.json's live_quotes map, and having score/stops reuse that cache before falling back to a second targeted fetch only for tickers the cache doesn't cover. Generalise: before adding a second price-fetch call anywhere in the pipeline, check whether an earlier stage this run already pulled the same ticker -- the orchestrator's own live_quotes map (added 2026-08-07, G32) already exists for exactly this reuse and was underused.",
