      "text": "smith-ledger's initial email search returns truncated snippets that cut off before the Shares:/Order Type: fields, forcing a second round-trip get_thread call per truncated result -- on the 2026-09-01 19-ticker reconciliation, 12 of 23 found confirmations needed a follow-up full-thread fetch, i.e. roughly half its 48 tool calls were this second pass. Fixed 2026-09-01: smith-ledger.md now instructs requesting a longer snippet / full body on the INITIAL search_threads call for INDmoney transaction-confirmation searches specifically (these are short, templated emails -- a longer snippet costs little and usually captures the whole confirmation in one call), rather than defaulting to a short snippet and conditionally following up. Generalise: for any email search whose target field is known to sit past the default snippet cutoff on a predictable email template, request more text upfront rather than paying for a conditional second call on most results.",
