      "text": "CORRECTION to the prior lesson (idx 7): 'request a longer snippet on the initial search' is not achievable -- search_threads' snippet field is a fixed Gmail-provided field with no length parameter; the tool schema has no such knob. The real fix is process, not a request parameter: smith-ledger.md's own step 3 already knew the snippet 'almost always' truncates before Shares:/Order Type: and calls the get_thread follow-up 'not optional' -- so treating it as a CONDITIONAL check-then-fetch (search, read snippet, decide it's insufficient, then fetch) wastes a full reasoning pass per row on a decision whose answer is already known. Fixed 2026-09-01: smith-ledger.md now skips the snippet-sufficiency check for BUY/SELL confirmation threads specifically and goes straight to a batch of get_thread calls for every thread search_threads returns, since experience says the snippet is insufficient essentially every time for this specific email template. This does not reduce the total get_thread call count (still ~1 per confirmation) but removes a wasted per-row snippet-inspection decision step, and lets the follow-up fetches be issued as one clearly-planned batch instead of a conditional loop. Generalise: when a fallback path fires on close to 100% of rows for a known reason, stop treating it as a fallback and make it the default path -- the branch that never gets taken is pure overhead.",
