      "date": "2026-09-01",
      "kind": "correction",
      "text": "Extended the pull-once principle (idx for the price-fetch lesson) beyond prices to two more confirmed duplications, both found by inspecting actual 2026-09-01 run data rather than guessing: (1) smith-watchlist independently fetched analyst target prices with zero cache awareness, even though smith-signals already populates data_cache.analyst_targets for every holding as a free byproduct of a call it makes anyway -- roughly a third of any watchlist slice overlaps with current holdings (AVGO/NVDA/MU/ASML/TER/TSM/GEV/INTC/GOOG recurred in both smith-signals' analyst_targets_updates AND smith-watchlist's target-gap setups on the SAME run). Fixed: smith-watchlist.md now checks the embedded analyst_targets cache first, same pattern as its existing earnings_calendar check. (2) SKILL.md section 2.9's scheduled-run email-search fallback and section 3's LEDGER trigger both fire off the identical signal (qty_changes non-empty) and, as written, both would run their own search_threads for the same from:transactions.indmoney.com query on the same run -- avoided today only by orchestrator judgment, not by anything in the file. Fixed: 2.9's fallback now explicitly skips entirely whenever smith-ledger was dispatched. Generalise: when auditing for duplicated pulls, don't stop at the first instance found (prices) -- check every OTHER external-data-fetching agent pair for the same shape (two things wanting the same fact, dispatched close enough in time that neither knows the other already has it).",
